Zine Installation Instructions
==============================

Zine requires Python 3.12, 3.13, or 3.14.  Runtime dependencies are declared
in ``pyproject.toml`` and are installed automatically by standard Python
packaging tools.

Installation
------------

Create a virtual environment and install Zine from a source checkout::

    $ python3 -m venv .venv
    $ .venv/bin/python -m pip install .

An editable development installation, including test and documentation tools,
can be created with::

    $ .venv/bin/python -m pip install -e '.[test,docs]'

The same environment can be created with uv::

    $ uv sync --all-extras

The installation provides ``zine-server``, ``zine-shell``,
``zine-reset-instance``, ``zine-create-apache-config``, and
``zine-regenerate-post-uids`` commands.  The matching scripts under
``scripts/`` can still be run directly from a source checkout.

Deployment
----------

Create a writable instance directory and point a WSGI server at
``zine.get_wsgi_app``::

    from zine import get_wsgi_app

    application = get_wsgi_app('/var/lib/zine/yourblog')

A mod_wsgi template is available as ``servers/zine.wsgi``.  CGI and optional
FastCGI templates are provided for compatible hosting environments, although
CGI is not recommended for production use.  Open the instance URL and follow
the web setup instructions to create its database and administrator account.

Development Quickstart
----------------------

For a quickstart with the Werkzeug development server::

    $ mkdir instance
    $ uv run zine-server -I instance

After the first start, the web setup wizard creates the database tables and an
administrator account.  To open a Python console with the instance context::

    $ uv run zine-shell -I instance

Run the regression suite and build the API documentation with::

    $ uv run --extra test pytest
    $ uv run --extra docs sphinx-build -W -b html api api/_build/html
